{
  "_comment": [
    "BrainSaw installations, transcribed from Rob's tracking spreadsheet (2026-08-09).",
    "A *site* is a lab or facility at one location; a site may hold several *systems*.",
    "Publications belong to the site, not to an individual system, because users of a",
    "site generally use whichever of its systems is free.",
    "",
    "Stalled entries are deliberately absent. A system only appears once money has been",
    "committed and work is under way — 'under discussion but stalled' is a twinkle in the",
    "eye, not an installation. Left out for that reason: Han lab (Wuhan), CSHL, Trondheim.",
    "",
    "'systemsName' is used only by sites with more than one system, to head their",
    "publication list: 'Publications from SWC systems'. Only SWC and Crick have several.",
    "",
    "'microscope' and 'selfBuilt' are kept because they are real data, but nothing displays",
    "them: the differences between systems are not meaningful to a visitor. Bring them back",
    "when there is a distinction worth drawing, such as the coming cryostat variant.",
    "E-mail addresses are deliberately not included; contact names are derived from them.",
    "",
    "Photographs are real, supplied by Rob, down-sized by tools/make_thumbs.py. Systems we",
    "have no photograph of carry 'photoStandIn': true and show the Nerf ZombieStrike",
    "BrainSaw instead — obviously not a microscope, which is the point: it reads as a gap",
    "to be filled rather than as a picture of that system."
  ],

